---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';

const compares = [
  { href: '/compare/datadog',   name: 'vs Datadog',   note: 'Investigation built in, pricing you can predict' },
  { href: '/compare/splunk',    name: 'vs Splunk',    note: 'A SIEM that investigates, not just searches' },
  { href: '/compare/grafana',   name: 'vs Grafana',   note: 'Integrated platform vs assembled stack' },
  { href: '/compare/pagerduty', name: 'vs PagerDuty', note: 'A page that arrives already investigated' },
  { href: '/compare/elastic',   name: 'vs Elastic',   note: 'Investigation without operating a cluster' },
];

const alternatives = [
  { href: '/blog/betterstack-alternative', name: 'BetterStack alternative', note: 'Uptime + logs, honestly compared' },
  { href: '/blog/uptimerobot-alternative', name: 'UptimeRobot alternative', note: 'When you outgrow a pure uptime checker' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do your comparison pages play fair with competitors?',
    a: 'That is the rule we hold ourselves to. Every comparison opens by acknowledging what the other tool genuinely does well — and several of them are excellent, category-leading products. We never quote competitor pricing (it changes and varies by deal), we do not invent weaknesses, and we say plainly when a competitor is the better choice for a given team. A comparison that pretends the incumbent has no strengths is not worth your time, and it would not survive contact with your own evaluation anyway.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What actually makes 24Observe different across all of these?',
    a: 'One idea runs through every comparison: detection and display are not the hard part — investigation is. Most tools collect telemetry beautifully and leave you to investigate by hand. 24Observe investigates every incident with an AI analyst that returns a verdict with evidence. Around that sit consolidation (one platform, one bill), first-class AI-agent coverage, an agent-programmable API, and the option to self-host. Those are the threads you will see repeated, because they are the real differences.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is 24Observe more mature than these incumbents?',
    a: 'No, and we will not claim it. Datadog, Splunk, Grafana, PagerDuty, and Elastic are mature products with large ecosystems and long track records at scale. 24Observe is younger and more focused; its capabilities are real and deployed, but we describe what it does rather than implying adoption we have not earned. Where maturity or breadth is the deciding factor, we say so on the relevant page.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I evaluate 24Observe alongside my current tool?',
    a: 'Yes, and we recommend it. 24Observe ingests open standards (OpenTelemetry) and webhook sources, and exports cleanly via signed webhooks and a gap-free export, so you can run it next to what you have, move one painful surface across, and judge the difference on your own incidents. You do not have to commit to a migration to test the claims on these pages.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which comparison should I read first?',
    a: 'Read the one for the tool you are weighing us against. If you are choosing a broad observability suite, start with Datadog or Grafana; for SIEM, Splunk or Elastic; for incident response and on-call, PagerDuty. Each is self-contained and honest about where each product fits. If you are coming from a pure uptime tool, the BetterStack and UptimeRobot pieces are the closest fit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if my tool isn’t listed here?',
    a: 'The same principles apply regardless. Ask: after an alert fires, who does the investigation? Is the pricing predictable as I grow? How many separate tools and bills am I consolidating? Are AI agents covered? Can I self-host if I need to? Those questions will tell you more about fit than any feature checklist — and they are the questions every page here is organised around.',
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Compare 24Observe vs Datadog, Splunk and more"
  description="Honest, fair comparisons against Datadog, Splunk, Grafana, PagerDuty, and Elastic — plus how to actually evaluate an observability and security platform."
  activeNav={null}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-bg"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-left">
          <div class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span> Compare</div>
          <h1 class="h1">Honest comparisons — <em>including where the other tool wins.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Most comparison pages are thinly-disguised sales copy that pretend the incumbent has no strengths. These are
            not that. Datadog, Splunk, Grafana, PagerDuty, and Elastic are, in their categories, excellent — and each
            comparison says so before explaining where 24Observe differs and who each is right for. Read the one that
            matches your decision, or start with how to think about the choice at all.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-ctas">
            <a href="https://login.24observe.com/register" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Start free <span class="arr">→</span></a>
            <a href="#how" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">How to choose</a>
          </div>
